<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Viet Minh force the surrender of the French garrison at Dien Bien Phu</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/suriname"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Suriname.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Suriname</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Suriname becomes an autonomous country within the Kingdom of the Netherlands</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-honduras"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Honduras.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Honduras</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The great banana strike wins workers the right to organise</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-guatemala"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Guatemala.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Guatemala</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A CIA-backed invasion forces Árbenz to resign</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-algeria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Algeria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Algeria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The FLN launches the war of independence on 1 November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/french-indochina"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/French%20Indochina.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>French Indochina</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Defeat at Dien Bien Phu and the Geneva Accords end French Indochina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-paraguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Paraguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Paraguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Alfredo Stroessner seizes power and rules until 1989</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/civil-rights-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Civil%20rights%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Civil rights movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Supreme Court rules segregated public schools unconstitutional in Brown v. Board of Education</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/yangshao-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Yangshao%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Yangshao culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Yangshao culture is estimated to be more than 1,000 years older than the Anau culture, weakening Andersson’s theory of a western origin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/great-pyramid-of-giza"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Great%20Pyramid%20of%20Giza.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Great Pyramid of Giza</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Kamal el-Mallakh finds a sealed boat pit at the south foot of the pyramid holding the dismantled Khufu ship</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/dead-sea-scrolls"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dead%20Sea%20Scrolls.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dead Sea Scrolls</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Four scrolls advertised in The Wall Street Journal were bought for Israel for $250,000</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Viet Minh defeat the French at the Battle of Dien Bien Phu, and the Geneva Accords divide Vietnam provisionally along the 17th parallel</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Geneva Conference agreement provides for the withdrawal of Viet Minh and French forces from Cambodia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/ho-chi-minh"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ho%20Chi%20Minh.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ho Chi Minh</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Việt Minh defeat the French at Điện Biên Phủ; the Geneva Accords divide Vietnam at the 17th parallel</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/pali-canon"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pali%20Canon.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pali Canon</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sixth Council Tipiṭaka is published at Rangoon, in 40 volumes in Burmese script</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Viet Minh assault begins with an attack on the northeastern outpost of Béatrice</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Algerian battalion on Gabrielle falls back, abandoning the northern outpost to the Viet Minh</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Massed Viet Minh assaults open on Dominique and Eliane in the central camp</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Viet Minh overrun Huguette 1 and take control of more than 90 percent of the airfield</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Giáp orders an all-out attack and the remaining French positions are overrun</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/kaifeng"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kaifeng.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kaifeng</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The capital of Henan province moves to Zhengzhou</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Anvil clears Nairobi of Kikuyu, Embu and Meru, and villagisation begins in June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/populism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Populism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Populism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Edward Shils in the United States and Hélio Jaguaribe in Brazil publish the texts that turn populism into an academic concept</span></li></ul></section>
